# Generated science index: `khai-tests science build` writes docs/SCIENCE.md
# from every misfit's REFERENCE.md Origin table, and its build-drift gate holds
# it byte-identical to that build. Prettier reformatting it would fight the gate,
# and its style is machine-written, not hand-authored.
#
# Both spellings, because this pattern is ANCHORED: a slash anywhere but the end
# binds it to this file's own directory, so `docs/SCIENCE.md` stops matching the
# day the index moves to packages/khai-misfits/docs/. Nothing announces that. The
# file simply becomes formattable, and the trap closes both ways -- leave it and
# `format:check` fails, which is the FIRST step of the khai-tests job so CI reads
# red while `npm test` is green; format it and the drift gate fails saying the
# index is out of date, which is a false diagnosis, since it is not stale, it has
# been reformatted. One cause, two red lights, and neither names it.
docs/SCIENCE.md
packages/*/docs/SCIENCE.md
